&lt;p&gt;As a Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity help craft in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to create and iterate player-focused designs that will delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Game Designer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;on Riftbound, you&#39;ll report to a Game Design Manager and work directly with other designers. You will design and improve the gameplay experience through the lens of game rules and their interactions with content: cards. Primary among your responsibilities will be working with set designers to build, improve, and execute on new mechanics, templates, and rules, and you will also be expected to contribute to card design across many products, and support other efforts related to the Riftbound game experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the relevant audiences for the game, and from this, calibrate your design expertise to reflect appropriate taste for these audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and sense-making to identify opportunities to improve the health of the game through cards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Articulate and consider a scope and depth of possible solutions, including possible effects, and collaboratively reach the best solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and improve rules across the game’s design and execution, especially understanding the multiple ways the game will be played by players&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve existing design frameworks, our approaches to design, and create new ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openly share work and seek feedback from other developers, while combine co-worker and player feedback to calibrate design direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide mentorship to more junior members of the design team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years experience as a game designer and/or tabletop game rules manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working on rules for tabletop games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad mechanics and content design ability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of CCGs and their features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience playing or judging in CCGs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or playing PvP strategy games&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing a competitive or multiplayer game&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For this role, you&#39;ll find success through craft expertise and a collaborative spirit that prioritizes the delight of players. We will look at your past studies and experience, but for this role, we also look for dedicated people with a personal relationship with games. If you embody player empathy and care about players&#39; experiences, this is the role for you!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Riot focuses on work/life balance, shown by our open paid time off policy and other perks such as flexible work schedules. We offer medical, dental, and life insurance, parental leave for you, your spouse/domestic partner, and children, and a 401k with company match. Check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/work-with-us/overview&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;benefits pages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Riot Games, we&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/who-we-are/values&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.riotgames.com/en/who-we-are/values&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;put players first&lt;/a&gt;. That mission drives ever

&lt;p&gt;As a Principal Game Designer, you will design, tweak, and optimize the player experience. Your analytical skills, player insight, and creativity aid in crafting in- and out-of-game experiences that engage and surprise players. You will collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and work with every tool at hand to innovate and iterate player-focused designs that&#39;ll delight millions around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://playvalorant.com/en-us/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VALORANT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is Riot’s take on a character-based tactical shooter. As a &lt;strong&gt;Principal Game Designer&lt;/strong&gt; on the &lt;strong&gt;Competitive Systems team&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll help shape and define how players engage with competition across ranked, matchmaking, and adjacent systems that influence mastery, fairness, and long-term growth. You’ll partner with product managers, engineers, analysts, and other designers to develop systems that are strategically sound, motivating to engage with, and worthy of players’ investment over time. You have significant competitive multiplayer affinity and experience, understanding the challenges players encounter and the motivations that drive them. You are comfortable operating in ambiguous spaces and can design and iterate on solutions to complex systemic problems. This role reports to the Lead Metasystems Designer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve competitive systems that reward player skill, growth, and long-term investment in VALORANT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the design of ranked, matchmaking, and adjacent competitive systems to support fairness, competitive integrity, and player engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product managers, engineers, analysts, and design leadership to ensure systems are cohesive, consistent, and in line with VALORANT’s overall vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the focus on player value by leveraging feedback, research, and game data to iterate on designs and improve the competitive experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create multiple design solutions and clearly articulate the trade-offs, risks, and player impact of each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direction, mentorship, and feedback to other designers, fostering collaboration and craft excellence across systems design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Playtest VALORANT regularly and help push improvements for existing systems and new concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in professional Game Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience developing competitive multiplayer systems such as matchmaking, ranked, and skill systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped or contributed to at least one AAA+ online competitive title.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design and iterate on complex systems with a clear understanding of player impact and downstream effects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills with proven ability to articulate design rationale, trade-offs, and decision frameworks to cross-disciplinary partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a live-service development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep passion for and understanding of competitive online games and their player communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with online shooters, especially VALORANT or tactical shooters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience balancing competitive integrity with engaging and rewarding systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a senior craft leader or thought partner on materially impactful design initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret and learn from charged or emotional player feedback to improve the product experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing across multiple platforms, including PC, console, or mobile.&lt;/li&g

&lt;p&gt;At Riot, we believe in putting players first. Our Sydney-based team is partnering globally to build next-generation features and technology on an exciting Unpublished R&amp;amp;D Title. The team focuses on supporting the game&#39;s visual targets and content production needs - helping our artists to realize a vibrant and rich world for players to be immersed and express themselves in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Technical Artist, Tools &amp;amp; Pipeline, you’ll shape the creative engine that powers our teams - defining and elevating end-to-end workflows across disciplines including Character Art, Animation, Environment Art, Audio, and VFX. You’ll be a strategic partner to artists, Technical Art, and Engineering, evaluating tools and pipelines, clarifying production requirements, and ensuring our workflows enable creativity at scale. Your work will directly impact how ideas move from concept to shipped content, empowering multiple teams to operate efficiently in parallel production streams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll help stand up and sustain scalable tools and processes, providing hands-on technical support while gathering data and feedback to continuously improve the artist experience. You’ll build strong cross-disciplinary relationships to uncover pain points and guide meaningful system and pipeline improvements. As an active member of Riot’s Technical Art community, you’ll mentor fellow TAs, contribute to craft growth, and foster a culture of knowledge sharing through clear documentation and open feedback. By setting clear goals, offering actionable direction, and championing continuous improvement, you’ll ensure our workflows not only support today’s production but evolve to meet the ambitions of tomorrow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Manager, Technical Art, and work closely with the Tech Art Director and other members of the team abroad.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and level up the end-to-end workflow for our many creative disciplines, such as Character Art, Animation, Environment Art, Audio, and VFX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Technical Art and Engineering partners to support artist needs, including evaluating tools and workflows, and communicating requirements for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help stand up and maintain scalable artist tools and workflows to support multiple teams in parallel production streams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support to artists working from our art workflows, collecting data to further improve the tools they are using, making recommendations and improvements where necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an active member of the Tech Art community within Riot, participate in craft-focused meetings and events, and actively mentor for other Technical Artists in their craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build close relationships with artists and engineers to understand needs, identify pain points, and help guide workflow, pipeline, and system improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spread knowledge of the team’s processes through documentation and help teams expand their technical know-how&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently give and take constructive feedback, direct next steps, and communicate clear goals and outcomes to your team&lt;/li&gt;
